Based on an algorithm that [http://groups.google.com/group/lojban/msg/81593c27375203a9|xorxes suggested], from the idea ((another approach to cultural fu'ivla|suggested here)), I created a python script that, given a list of ISO codes, and their meanings, can generate not only the new fu'ivla, but also a jbovlaste-ready definition.
For example:

||gugde'alu | $x_1$ is the country with the code ISO-3166 ''AL'' (Albania) for people $x_2$. | gugde | Albania | the country with ISO-3166 code ''AL''||

I've done tables for:

*((Countries|ISO generated fu'ivla for countries))
*((Currencies|ISO generated fu'ivla for currencies))
*((Languages|ISO generated fu'ivla for languages))
